  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we just take the constant out of the derivative and use the result for the derivative of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-{csc}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡x}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
